{ Your pawn wants to run, but his king is standing in its way. Move his king off that square. }
1. Rd7+ { A check that shoves his king right off the pawn's column. [%csl Gd7][%cal Gc6c8][%tail] } (1. Kb7 { You walk the king out, and the checks start at once. } 1... Rb2+ 2. Kc8 Ra2 { He holds you. Drawn. }) (1. Rc8 { The rook goes in front of its own pawn and falls asleep. } 1... Rb2+ 2. Ka5 Rb1 { Drawn. His rook checks from behind for ever, and your own blocks its own pawn's road. }) (1. Re7 { The rook steps right next to his king. } 1... Kxe7 { It is simply eaten. You are lost. }) (1. Ra7 { The same trouble on the other side. } 1... Rb2+ 2. Ka5 Kc5 { Lost. His king walks up beside the pawn, and your rook never even got behind it. }) (1. Kb5 { You walk away and leave the rook hanging. } 1... Kxc7 { The rook goes for free. You are lost. }) 1... Ke5 2. c7 2... Kf5 3. c8=Q { A new queen on c8. One check was all it took to clear the whole road. } 1-0


[Event "Rook endgames: block the last check"]
