[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/8/1k2P3/8/2K4r/3R4/8/8/8_w_-_-_0_1"]

{ His rook is checking you and your pawn needs one more move. Four legal moves. Pick. }
1. Rd5 { The rook steps in the way and offers a trade he cannot refuse. [%csl Gd5] } (1. Kd6 { Also winning: the king walks out of the check towards the pawn. } 1... Rh6+ { The checks go on, but you are still winning. }) (1. Kb4 { You run from the check and abandon the pawn. } 1... Re5 2. e8=Q Rxe8 { Drawn. Unescorted, the new queen falls at once. }) (1. Kc4 { The same mistake, one square across. } 1... Re5 2. e8=Q Rxe8 { Drawn. Undefended, the new queen lasts one move too. }) 1... Rxd5+ { He takes with check. Take back. } 2. Kxd5 { And nothing on the board can stop the pawn now. [%csl Gd5][%cal Ge7e8][%tail] } 2... Kc7 3. e8=Q { A new queen on e8, with his king still two squares short of it. } 1-0
